Game screen — map is small-ish but okay. Titles show weird letter-spacing artifacts (Cinzel not loaded? It uses fallback Georgia maybe okay). Actually labels "THE GODDES" fine.

Bugs visible:
- Map labels tiny/overlap ("ASHEN VEIL" etc), map letters maybe cut at edges? FROSTFALL label is cut off at right edge ("FROSTFALL" overflow). Map SVG overflow:visible, but clipped by board? It's cut at screen edge. Not huge.
- Battle card and buttons okay.
- Buttons "MARCH · 2 ESSENCE" wraps, text small; touch height ~45, okay but below 48px recommended.
- Large gap between map and battle card due to flex.
- Map board width 100%, height min(52vh,500) = 416, but SVG viewBox aspect 940x550 -> preserveAspectRatio default xMidYMid meet giving ~247px height centered, so map looks small. Set svg preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" but height auto? Could set map-board aspect-ratio 940/550 and height auto to fill width. For portrait, better to fill width.

Also mobile Android: `overflow:hidden` and fixed heights may clip with browser UI. Add dvh.

Other bugs to fix:
- Menu title clipping.
- Safe area insets (notch).
- Scenario: on very short screens, frame min-height 410 exceeds viewport. Set min-height:0 on mobile and let content scroll.
- Modal overflow when keyboard/small height.
- Toast nowrap overflow.
- Touch targets >=44px.
- Options modal: checkbox and range inputs; setting rows wrap? At 360, volume label + 135px input may fit 308 px; okay.
- Load Game disabled state.
- Game map: labels scaled; could increase font sizes on mobile since SVG scales down: 940 viewBox into 342 width -> 13px becomes 4.7px. That's why labels are tiny. Set `.territory-label{font-size:22px}` on mobile. Node r=8 -> 3px; okay maybe increase.
- Map board aspect ratio matching svg so no big empty space and larger map.
- The game bottom stacked on mobile already.

Also "too many bugs" maybe refers to overlaps/clipping. Let's do a thorough mobile pass.

Approach: restructure CSS with clean mobile-first overrides appended at end (so they win), replacing existing messy media queries? Better to keep desktop but add a consolidated, well-ordered `@media (max-width: 760px)` block at the end, and also `@media (max-height: 640px)`.

Specific changes:

Base:
- meta viewport: `width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover`.
- body/html: height:100%; height:100dvh; overflow:hidden; overscroll-behavior:none.
- `button{touch-action:manipulation}` and tap highlight.
- `.screen` height:100dvh? position fixed inset 0 works.

Menu portrait (<=520px):
- `.menu-wrap{width:100%;padding:max(24px,env(safe-area-inset-top)) 22px max(24px,env(safe-area-inset-bottom));justify-content:flex-end;padding-bottom:max(10vh, 40px)}` Hmm existing uses 35px and 12vh.
- `.title{font-size:clamp(26px,7.6vw,40px); margin-bottom:24px; max-width:100%}` Ensure "and The Conquest" fits: at 360 width minus 44 px padding = 316px. Text length ~16 chars at 0.55em avg width with letter spacing .045em: 16*0.57*fs ≈ 9.1fs; fs must <=34.7. So 8vw=28.8 fits. Why clipped earlier? clamp min 32px -> 32*9.1=291 <316. Hmm actually Cinzel average width maybe ~0.62 with spacing => 32*0.66*16 = 338 >316. So set font-size: clamp(24px, 7.2vw, 34px) -> 25.9px. Fine. Or allow span white-space normal? Keep nowrap but smaller.
- Menu width 100%, buttons 48px min-height, font 13px.
- Scene art on portrait: background shows castle/moon at right which is cropped; maybe reposition `svg` preserveAspectRatio slice already. It's okay.

Scenario portrait:
- `.scenario-screen{padding:max(10px,env(safe-area-inset-top)) 10px max(10px,env(safe-area-inset-bottom))}`
- `.scenario-frame{height:100%;min-height:0;}` grid rows auto minmax(0,1fr) auto.
- `.scenario-head{height:auto;min-height:56px;padding:8px 14px}`
- `.scenario-content{grid-template-columns:1fr;grid-template-rows:auto minmax(0,1fr);padding:10px;gap:8px;min-height:0}`
- scenario entry min-height 46.
- character panel: `overflow:hidden`.
- character card: switch to rows? Let's decide. With width 340 and height maybe 430 available (800 viewport - header 58 - footer 50 - paddings). If side-by-side: image ~105 wide, bio 200 wide at 10px. Small. Stacked: image banner 140 tall, bio 250 tall at 12px width 316 → ~6 lines? Text at 12px, 50 chars/line, 9 paragraphs ~ 900 chars → 18 lines + margins ≈ 350px, scroll. Better readability. I think stacked portrait layout is the right "portrait style".

But the user liked image beside bio? They asked earlier "di sampingnya" (beside it). On Android portrait, beside means narrow columns. Could keep side-by-side but with better font. Hmm "optimalkan untuk gaya potrait di android" — priority is usable. Maybe a hybrid: portrait on top as a 34% height banner with object-position top (face visible), bio below 12.5px, Next anchored. That's typical mobile character screen. I'd go with vertical stacking since it's explicitly Android portrait.

Alternative: use 2 columns only on wider (>600) and stack under 600. That respects both.

Character image: in stacked mode `height:clamp(120px,24vh,210px); object-position:center 18%`. The image is 683x1024 portrait; cropping to wide banner cuts body but face at top visible. `object-position:center 12%`.

- `.character-biography{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch}`
- Next full width 48px at bottom of copy; perhaps place button in footer instead? Keep in card but full width.

Footer: hint text small; may overflow "CHARACTER SELECTED: LUX OSBORN." at 9px fits. But with safe area.

Game portrait:
- `.game-ui{padding:calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 12px calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));gap:8px}`
- top: brand font 14px; stats 3 columns? Currently flex-wrap leads "REALMS" wrapping to second row; screenshot shows Day/Essence top and Realms below right. Could make stats grid 3 equal columns spanning width under brand, or keep. Better: game-top flex-direction column? Header brand + stats. On 360, brand 140 + stats 65*2 + gap = 140+130+20 = 290 fits first row; realms wraps. Cleaner: make `.game-top{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;}` and stats as 3 small chips in one row? At 360: brand ~120, stats 3*60=180 + gaps 12 = 192; 120+192=312 fits. So set stat min-width 56, padding 6px, font 8px, b 14px. Keep single row.
- Map: `.map-area{flex:1;min-height:0}` and `.map-board{width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:940/550;min-height:0;max-height:100%}`. But aspect ratio 1.7 wide in portrait gives 342x200 only. There's a lot of vertical space (gap in screenshot). Better make map-board fill available space with SVG `preserveAspectRatio` maybe "xMidYMid meet", so map height 200 leaves blank. Could rotate? No. Use `preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"` but board tall → centered map small. Alternative: change the SVG's `preserveAspectRatio` to "xMidYMid slice" with a tall board? That crops sides, bad.

