content.text:
Landscape 800x360 game is broken: map overflows vertically, battle card overlaps map, buttons overlapping map, save&return under. Our max-height rules didn't cover game. This is landscape though, user asked portrait. But "too many bugs" — we should at least make landscape not broken. The existing max-height 650 applies only min-width 701 with some game tweaks (map-board height 52vh = 187, game-ui gap 10). But screenshot shows map huge? map-board min 340 height and height min(550,62vh)=223 but min-height 340 wins. So 340 tall in 360 screen. Buttons at bottom overlay. Need fix for short landscape.

Add `@media (max-height:540px)`:
```css
.game-ui{padding:8px 14px;gap:6px}
.game-brand{font-size:14px}
.stat{padding:5px 9px;min-width:70px;font-size:8px}
.stat b{font-size:14px}
.map-board{height:min(44vh,190px);min-height:0;width:min(940px,72vw)}
.territory-label{font-size:16px}
.game-bottom{gap:8px}
.battle-card{min-width:min(300px,45vw);padding:8px 12px}
.battle-card h2{font-size:14px}
.battle-card p{font-size:10px}
.action-btn{min-height:38px;padding:8px 10px;font-size:10px}
.game-actions{gap:6px}
```
But at 800x360: map height 44vh=158; width min(940, 576)=576; aspect 1.7 => height 337 if width 576 with svg meet inside 158 -> map 158 tall. Fine. Battle card width 300. Buttons might not fit beside at 800? The current bottom is absolute? no, flex. bottom row: battle card ~300 + actions ~ 380 => 680 + padding 28 <800. Fits.

But map plus header (50) + bottom (80) = 288 < 360. Good.

Also the battle card currently overlaps because `.map-area{flex:1}` and map-board min-height 340 > area. Fixing min-height solves.

Yet landscape isn't required; still, easy.

Also in landscape 800x360, `.game-ui` left brand "THE GODDES / AND THE CONQUEST" wraps ok.

Check landscape menu.

